{"approved":false,"back_sample":null,"beam_size":2,"checks":{"no_residual_markers":true,"nonempty":true,"not_truncated":true,"protected_values":true,"translated":true},"context":"rlc-circuit-calculator UI copy.additionalFaqs.2.answer","detected_language":"es","format":"usefulverse-background-draft-v1","key":"rlc-circuit-calculator.copy.additionalFaqs.2.answer","keys":["rlc-circuit-calculator.copy.additionalFaqs.2.answer"],"locale":"es","model":"google/madlad400-3b-mt","raw_translation":"Para el modelo en serie, Q = ω₀L/R y el ancho de banda es R/(ZXQPH0000QXZπL). Para el modelo en paralelo, Q = R/(ω₀L) y el ancho de banda es ZXQPH0001QXZ/(ZXQPH0002QXZπRC).","record_id":"c6e6f6fef28a9ad12c533aec8bf6fda5bcc8d55c1b8eb089aea4007e07af32c2","revision":"fa184c675da0b5c9e1c8694fccd4e12e2d422094","run_id":"40843674935","seconds":1.9791785384999798,"source":"For the series model, Q = ω₀L/R and bandwidth is R/(2πL). For the parallel model, Q = R/(ω₀L) and bandwidth is 1/(2πRC). These are ideal single-resonance relationships.","source_commit":"e1f72394198c1a94fce448ea14cd79b496701273","source_hash":"d929113d31b49cd67fa0b70f4d3ec5403c3e4e89c98b4fcab359fb6074436c8a","status":"machine-draft","translation":"Para el modelo en serie, Q = ω₀L/R y el ancho de banda es R/(2πL). Para el modelo en paralelo, Q = R/(ω₀L) y el ancho de banda es 1/(2πRC).","truncated":false,"warnings":[]}
